  "question": {
    "text": "A simple pendulum doing small oscillations at a place R height above earth surface has time period of $T_1=4 \\mathrm{~s}$. $T_2$ would be it's time period if it is brought to a point which is at a height $2 R$ from earth surface. Choose the correct relation $[\\mathrm{R}=$ radius of Earth $]:$",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "YoXkw",
      "text": "$T_1=T_2$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "cTOOa",
      "text": "$2 \\mathrm{~T}_1=3 \\mathrm{~T}_2$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JFCNZ",
      "text": "$3 \\mathrm{~T}_1=2 \\mathrm{~T}_2$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "Gnwpk",
      "text": "$2 \\mathrm{~T}_1=\\mathrm{T}_2$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Time period of simple pendulum,\n$\\mathrm{T}=2 \\pi \\sqrt{\\frac{l}{\\mathrm{~g}}} \\& \\mathrm{~g}=\\frac{\\mathrm{GM}}{(\\mathrm{R}+\\mathrm{h})^2}$\n$\\therefore \\mathrm{T} \\propto(\\mathrm{R}+\\mathrm{h})$\n$\\Rightarrow \\frac{\\mathrm{T}_1}{\\mathrm{~T}_2}=\\frac{\\left(\\mathrm{R}+\\mathrm{h}_1\\right)}{\\left(\\mathrm{R}+\\mathrm{h}_2\\right)}=\\frac{(\\mathrm{R}+\\mathrm{R})}{(\\mathrm{R}+2 \\mathrm{R})}=\\frac{2}{3} \\Rightarrow 3 \\mathrm{~T}_1=2 \\mathrm{~T}_2$",
    "image": null
  },
